WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.590
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:15.440
Last time: work backwards · 9 + 3 = 12

3
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:22.260
Chapter 4 · Breaking Big Problems Into Small Ones

4
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:32.470
Ever felt a job was way too big?

5
00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:41.290
"Riya, please clean your room!"

6
00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:52.390
Toys, books, a messy bed… Oh no!

7
00:00:52.390 --> 00:01:05.350
Where do I even start? What would you do?

8
00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:18.120
Toys · Books · Bed: three small jobs

9
00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:32.390
One small job at a time → clean room!

10
00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:37.000
That trick is called DECOMPOSITION

11
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:48.530
Breaking a big problem into small parts

12
00:01:48.530 --> 00:02:00.260
A roti: one small bite at a time

13
00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:06.930
Small task = one job you can finish

14
00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:12.400
Big job: pack the school bag

15
00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:20.170
Books · Bottle · Lunch box · Pencil box

16
00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:33.010
Timetable → Books → Bottle → Lunch box

17
00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:45.490
Then decide: first, next, last

18
00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:53.750
Nani is here! Riya makes nimbu pani

19
00:02:53.750 --> 00:03:04.420
Squeeze → Water → Sugar → Pour & serve

20
00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:15.160
Serve first? Nothing to pour! Serve LAST

21
00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:21.960
Nani's puzzle: what is 23 + 45?

22
00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:30.780
23 = 20 + 3 · 45 = 40 + 5

23
00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:39.970
Tens: 20 + 40 = 60 · Ones: 3 + 5 = 8

24
00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:47.980
60 + 8 = 68!

25
00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:57.100
What is 6 × 14?

26
00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:05.390
Break it up: 14 = 10 + 4

27
00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:10.300
6 × 10 = 60 · 6 × 4 = 24

28
00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:18.670
60 + 24 = 84. So 6 × 14 = 84!

29
00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:28.130
Coders use decomposition every day!

30
00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:42.140
Pitch · Bat · Ball · Score

31
00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:55.160
Algorithms are built in small parts too

32
00:04:55.160 --> 00:05:13.030
Which is NOT part of cleaning a room?

33
00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:22.230
Fly a kite doesn't help clean the room!

34
00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:43.390
Party steps are mixed up! What's the order?

35
00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:58.230
Date → Guest list → Snacks → Set up & enjoy

36
00:05:58.230 --> 00:06:03.530
Your turn: practice check

37
00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:18.540
Break 'make a birthday card' into 4 steps

38
00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:38.100
Fold → Draw → Write → Sign & give

39
00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:44.480
Big job → small jobs

40
00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:47.210
Put the small jobs in order

41
00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:52.220
Do one small job at a time

42
00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:56.390
Algorithms & sums are built in parts

43
00:06:56.390 --> 00:07:04.910
Chapter 4 done!

44
00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:11.710
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
